[1mNAME[0m
     [1mls[0m – list directory contents

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
     [1mls[0m [[1m-@ABCFGHILOPRSTUWabcdefghiklmnopqrstuvwxy1%,[0m] [[1m--color[0m=[4mwhen[24m]
        [[1m-D[0m [4mformat[24m] [[4mfile[24m [4m...[24m]

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
     For each operand that names a [4mfile[24m of a type other than directory, [1mls[0m
     displays its name as well as any requested, associated information.  For
     each operand that names a [4mfile[24m of type directory, [1mls[0m displays the names
     of files contained within that directory, as well as any requested,
     associated information.

     If no operands are given, the contents of the current directory are
     displayed.  If more than one operand is given, non-directory operands are
     displayed first; directory and non-directory operands are sorted
     separately and in lexicographical order.

     The following options are available:

:[K[K     [1m-@[0m      Display extended attribute keys and sizes in long ([1m-l[0m) output.

     [1m-A[0m      Include directory entries whose names begin with a dot (‘[4m.[24m’)
             except for [4m.[24m and [4m..[24m.  Automatically set for the super-user unless
             [1m-I[0m is specified.

     [1m-B[0m      Force printing of non-printable characters (as defined by
             ctype(3) and current locale settings) in file names as \[4mxxx[24m,
             where [4mxxx[24m is the numeric value of the character in octal.  This
             option is not defined in IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

     [1m-C[0m      Force multi-column output; this is the default when output is to
             a terminal.

     [1m-D[0m [4mformat[24m
             When printing in the long ([1m-l[0m) format, use [4mformat[24m to format the
             date and time output.  The argument [4mformat[24m is a string used by
             strftime(3).  Depending on the choice of format string, this may
             result in a different number of columns in the output.  This
             option overrides the [1m-T[0m option.  This option is not defined in
             IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

     [1m-F[0m      Display a slash (‘/’) immediately after each pathname that is a
