     [1m-R[0m      [7mRecursively[27m list subdirectories encountered.

     [1m-S[0m      Sort by size (largest file first) before sorting the operands in
             lexicographical order.

     [1m-T[0m      When printing in the long ([1m-l[0m) format, display complete time
             information for the file, including month, day, hour, minute,
             second, and year.  The [1m-D[0m option gives even more control over the
             output format.  This option is not defined in IEEE Std
             1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

     [1m-U[0m      Use time when file was created for sorting or printing.  This
             option is not defined in IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

     [1m-W[0m      Display whiteouts when scanning directories.  This option is not
             defined in IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

     [1m-X[0m      When listing recursively, do not descend into directories that
             would cross file system boundaries.  More specifically, this
             option will prevent descending into directories that have a
             different device number.

     [1m-a[0m      Include directory entries whose names begin with a dot (‘[4m.[24m’).
